    "lawCode": "Amd §§3 & 7, Chap 296 of 1992",
    "lawSection": "Firefighters' Benevolent Association",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7273A\n\nSPONSOR: BASKIN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 296 of the laws of 1992 incorporating the Rescue\nVolunteer and Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association Inc., and provid-\ning for its powers and duties, in relation to the purpose of such corpo-\nration and the use of certain tax monies received\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nRelates to the purpose of such corporation and the use of certain tax\nmonies received by the Rescue Volunteer and Exempt Firemen's Benevolent\nAssociation Inc. in the town of Cheektowaga, Erie County.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends Sections 3 and 7 of chapter 296 of the laws of 1992\nincorporating the Rescue Volunteer and Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Asso-\nciation to expand the purposes of the corporation and clarify the\npermissible use of foreign fire insurance premium taxes in accordance\nwith those purposes.\n\nSection 2: Sets forth the effective date, with tax-related provisions\napplying to premiums received on and after January 1, 2026.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill has been introduced at the request of the Rescue Volunteer and\nExempt Firemen's Benevolent Association Inc. In enhancing the goals of\nthe Association, it is necessary to amend chapter 296 of the laws of\n1992 to include language that specifies how aid and assistance can be\nused by volunteer members of the association and to reflect the broader\npurposes of health, safety, welfare, and morale support for its members\nand their families\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2023/24: A.10657 - Referred to Local Governments\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided however, that the\namendments to section 7 of chapter 296 of the laws of 1992 relating to\nincorporating the Rescue Volunteer and Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Asso-\nciation Inc., made by section one of this act, shall apply to taxes due\non premiums received on and after January 1, 2026.\n",
